truths.details:
Supersedes/corrects the contradicted hypothesis b42.item-script.type-not-itemtype (which claimed legacy item blocks use `Type = Normal` and that ItemType=base:X causes silent load failure). Both claims are false in B42.18.

Vanilla B42.18 (live install grep, media/scripts/, 1004 .txt files): 0 occurrences of `Type =` as a field assignment; 5105 `ItemType =` assignments; 5092 legacy `item Foo {}` blocks ALL using `ItemType = base:X` (alarmclock, animal, clothing, container, drainable, food, key, literature, map, moveable, normal, radio, weapon, weaponpart).

Canonical form:
module MyMod {
    item MyItem {
        DisplayName = My Item,
        ItemType = base:normal,
        Weight = 0.1,
    }
}

Runtime (pz-temp dedicated, fresh-vanilla + MasterySystem): getScriptManager():getItem('MasterySystem.UniversalKey') returned a registered, fully-populated item (displayName 'Universal Key', module 'MasterySystem'). The MasteryItems.txt legacy block with ItemType=base:normal loaded without silent failure.

PZ B42 server iterates every loaded recipe during client join and calls getResult().getType() on each. If any recipe has null Result (from B41 code references, renamed items like Base.Stone→Base.Stone2, or missing result items), the entire RecipePacket NPEs and every client cannot join.

Fix: add shims at the top of any file using Recipe.OnCreate/OnTest/GetItemTypes:
```lua
Recipe = Recipe or {}
Recipe.OnCreate = Recipe.OnCreate or {}
Recipe.OnTest = Recipe.OnTest or {}
Recipe.GetItemTypes = Recipe.GetItemTypes or {}
```
Also update renamed item IDs (Base.Stone→Base.Stone2, Base.WoodenStick→Base.WoodenStick2, Base.TreeBranch→Base.TreeBranch2).
